"- Copper Conductor Strand (Green Insulated)\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A stranded copper conductor encased in a green insulating layer, appearing as a circular cross-section with visible copper strands at the center.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - The insulating layer is primarily green with a yellowish tint near the center, while the exposed copper strands are metallic brownish-orange.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The cross-sectional diameter is approximately equal to the other conductor strands, fitting within the circular arrangement; exact length not discernible.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - The conductor is made of copper, and the insulation is a polymer or rubber-like material.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of multiple fine copper wires twisted together, surrounded by a green insulating sheath.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One instance.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Positioned at the top of the circular arrangement, above the blue and brown insulated strands.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The cross-section is viewed directly from above, with the conductor strands radiating outward from the center.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The conductor is embedded within the white/off-white insulation layer and is not visibly connected to any external components.\n\n- Copper Conductor Strand (Brown Insulated)\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A stranded copper conductor encased in a brown insulating layer, appearing as a circular cross-section with visible copper strands at the center.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - The insulating layer is a uniform brownish-gray color, with the exposed copper strands appearing metallic brownish-orange.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The cross-sectional diameter is approximately equal to the other conductor strands, fitting within the circular arrangement; exact length not discernible.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - The conductor is made of copper, and the insulation is a polymer or rubber-like material.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - Composed of multiple fine copper wires twisted together, surrounded by a brown insulating sheath.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One instance.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Positioned at the bottom right of the circular arrangement, adjacent to the blue insulated strand.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The cross-section is viewed directly from above, with the conductor strands radiating outward from the center.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The conductor is embedded within the white/off-white insulation layer and is not visibly connected to any external components.\n\n- Cable Insulation Layer (White/Off-white)\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A continuous, thick, circular layer of insulation material surrounding the three copper conductor strands.\n    - Attribute 2 Color - White or off-white with slight discoloration and speckles, appearing somewhat aged or weathered.\n    - Attribute 3 Size - The layer forms a complete circular boundary around the three conductor strands, with a thickness that appears consistent throughout the visible section.\n    - Attribute 4 Material - Likely a polymer-based insulation material such as PVC or rubber.\n    - Attribute 5 Composition - A solid, uniform layer designed to electrically isolate the conductors from each other and from the outer environment.\n    - Attribute 6 Quantity - One continuous layer.\n    - Attribute 7 Relative Location - Envelops all three copper conductor strands, forming the outermost layer of the cable cross-section.\n    - Attribute 8 Orientation - The layer is viewed from the top, appearing as a circular ring surrounding the central conductors.\n    - Attribute 9 Connection or Attachments - The layer is directly attached to and encapsulates the three conductor strands, forming a cohesive unit.\n\n- Copper Conductor Strand (Blue Insulated)\n    - Attribute 1 Type - A stranded copper conductor encased in a blue insulating layer, appearing as a circular cross-section with